Package: catmech
Title: Auditable Model-Based Imputation and Category Sensitivity
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: person("Patrick", "Iben", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "patrickiben@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-2443-7973"))
Description: Auditable completion of a continuous measurement using Gaussian
    models, predictive mean matching, an explicitly measured internal reference
    subset, or a reference-calibrated contamination model of the recorded values.
    Supports flag masking, optional exact or fallible interval categories,
    posterior draws and per-record corruption probabilities, convergence and
    donor-support diagnostics, reference hold-out checks, finite-scenario
    sensitivity comparisons and 'mice' analysis adapters. Retains a separate
    retain-or-replace sensitivity engine. Implements multiple-imputation
    combining rules and finite-sample degrees of freedom following Rubin (1987)
    <doi:10.1002/9780470316696> and Barnard and Rubin (1999)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/86.4.948>, and an unvalidated audit-size planning aid
    based on two-phase sampling theory (Neyman 1938)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1938.10503378>. Does not identify measurement error
    without assumptions or reference information, or guarantee coverage under
    misspecification.
